     "type": "intro",
     "title": "What If One Idea Was Worth $250,000?",
     "content": "A Fortune 500 VP calls you. Her division is bleeding talent. Turnover is at 38%. Each lost manager costs the company about $400,000 in replacement and ramp time.\n\nYou spend three weeks with her team. You diagnose the real problem — not pay, but a broken promotion path. You redesign the path. Twelve months later, turnover is 11%.\n\n**How much was that engagement worth?**\n\nAlan Weiss says: not the 90 hours you billed. Not even $1,000/hour. It was worth a slice of what you saved — and that slice could easily be $250,000.\n\nThis is **Million Dollar Consulting** — the model Weiss has taught for 40 years to thousands of solo consultants who now earn more than most law firm partners, work fewer hours, and answer to no boss. This lesson is the foundation: why hours are a trap, why value is the answer, and why one person with the right mindset can build a seven-figure practice from a spare bedroom.",
