     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Solo Consulting Model",
     "content": "Weiss built his practice without partners, without offices, without staff. He calls it the **solo practitioner model** — and he argues it is the highest-leverage business a knowledge worker can build.\n\n**Why solo works:**\n• **Zero overhead drag** — no rent, no payroll, no benefits eating margin\n• **Full margin capture** — every dollar of fee minus your expenses is yours\n• **Lifestyle compounding** — you choose clients, projects, calendar\n• **Speed of decision** — no committees, no partners to convince\n• **Reputation concentration** — the brand is YOU, not a firm\n\n**The trade-off:** there is no one to hide behind. Your name is on every proposal. Your judgment closes every deal. Your delivery defines every reference.\n\nWeiss's claim: a solo consultant with the right positioning can clear **$500K to $2M/year** working 100-150 billable days, with the rest spent on writing, speaking, travel, and family. The leverage is not headcount — it's **intellectual property and fee structure**.",
