     "type": "example",
     "title": "The $7,500 vs. $75,000 Story",
     "content": "A mid-size manufacturer's COO calls a consultant: their plant supervisors keep missing safety targets. OSHA citations are mounting.\n\n**Consultant A — hourly model:**\n• Quotes $250/hour, estimates 30 hours\n• Delivers a 40-page safety audit\n• Bills $7,500 plus expenses\n• Client files the report, OSHA fines continue, supervisors don't change behavior\n• Consultant moves on\n\n**Consultant B — value model:**\n• Spends 60 minutes asking the COO: *'What is one fewer OSHA citation worth? What is one avoided injury worth?'*\n• COO answers: each citation is ~$80K in fines + legal; each injury averages $250K in claims + lost productivity\n• Consultant proposes: a 90-day supervisor coaching program with a target of zero citations and zero lost-time injuries\n• Fee: **$75,000**, paid 50% up front\n• Delivers coaching, behavior tools, weekly check-ins\n• At day 90: zero citations, zero injuries, COO is a hero\n\nSame consultant could have done both. The COO's check-signing pen didn't change. The framing of the work — and the fee — did. **Consultant B walked away with 10x the income and a delighted client who refers two peers.**",
