     "explanation": "Weiss's premise says you must reframe the conversation BEFORE giving a fee. Quoting an hourly rate concedes the entire pricing model — and you'll be compared on rate, not value. The peer-mindset response is to politely redirect toward the buyer's business outcome. If they refuse to have that conversation, they're not the economic buyer and the engagement won't close at peer fees anyway.",
