     "explanation": "The economic buyer measures your fee against a multi-million-dollar business outcome. An HR or training contact measures the same fee against a department budget. The same proposal looks 'expensive' to one person and 'a no-brainer' to the other — not because the work changed, but because the reference frame changed. Weiss: *'Selling to anyone other than the economic buyer is malpractice against your own income.'*",
