     "explanation": "The right move is twofold: re-anchor on the agreed VALUE (not the fee) and offer a smaller SCOPE at a different price point. Splitting the difference signals the original fee was inflated. Adding a time-based discount creates artificial urgency that erodes trust. Saying 'not possible' closes a door that doesn't need to close. Weiss's principle: never discount the fee, always adjust the scope — and always re-anchor against the value number you already agreed on.",
