     "type": "example",
     "title": "A Real Two-Page Proposal That Closed for $425K",
     "content": "Here's an abbreviated version of an actual Weiss-style proposal that closed at **$425,000** in 9 days. (Client and consultant details anonymized.)\n\n**SITUATION APPRAISAL.** TalentForge, a $280M SaaS company, has experienced 34% engineering attrition over the past 18 months, costing an estimated $11M in replacement, ramp, and project delay. Leadership has stabilized but the talent system remains fragile heading into a planned IPO in Q4 2026.\n\n**OBJECTIVES.**\n• Reduce voluntary engineering attrition to under 12% within 12 months\n• Establish a manager-quality system that survives leadership transitions\n• Deliver a defensible talent narrative to public-market investors\n\n**MEASURES OF SUCCESS.**\n• HRIS report: voluntary attrition at month 12\n• Manager NPS survey (current baseline 22) reaches 60+\n• Investor materials accepted by underwriter's due diligence team\n\n**VALUE TO TALENTFORGE.** Eliminating 22 of the past year's 34 voluntary departures would save $7M in direct replacement cost and an estimated additional $4M in project delay. Successful IPO talent narrative supports a valuation multiple of approximately +0.5x revenue (~$140M of equity value).\n\n**METHODOLOGY AND OPTIONS.**\n*Option 1 — Diagnostic & Recommendations ($175K):* 8 weeks. Manager interviews, attrition pattern analysis, system redesign recommendations.\n*Option 2 — Diagnostic + Implementation ($300K) [RECOMMENDED]:* 6 months. All of Option 1 plus rollout coaching, manager calibration sessions, monthly progress reviews.\n*Option 3 — Diagnostic + Implementation + IPO Talent Narrative ($425K):* 12 months. All of Option 2 plus investor-materials development and rehearsal coaching for CEO/CHRO.\n\n**TIMING.** Start within 14 days of acceptance. Phase 1 complete in 8 weeks. Phase 2 monthly milestones for 4 months. Phase 3 quarterly.\n\n**JOINT ACCOUNTABILITIES.** Consultant provides expertise, frameworks, and direct facilitation. Client provides access to all engineering managers, HR data, and one named project sponsor at SVP level.\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS.** Selected fee payable 50% on acceptance, 50% at day 90. Expenses billed monthly at cost. Non-disclosure mutual. Professional fee non-refundable.\n\n**ACCEPTANCE.** ____________________ Date __________\n\n**Result:** CEO selected Option 3. Signed in 9 days. Closed at $425K plus expenses.",
