     "explanation": "Weiss's rule is absolute: no conceptual agreement, no proposal. The proposal is not a sales document — it's a summation of an agreement already reached verbally with the economic buyer. Sending proposals before the three locks are in place produces long, complicated documents that get pushed to committees, compared on price, and lost. Doing unpaid weeks of diagnostic work is also wrong — that's free consulting that erodes your fee positioning.",
