     "explanation": "Sponsor enthusiasm peaks on close-out day — that's the moment to ask. Weiss documents that consultants who ask for a referral and provide a draft testimonial on the day of close-out convert 3-4x as often as those who wait. The thank-you dinner is fine but secondary. Long emails get ignored. Waiting three months is fatal — by then the sponsor's daily attention has moved on, the change has become 'just how we work,' and the consultant's role in it has faded from memory. Two specific asks, made warmly, on the day of close-out.",
