     "explanation": "$700K is the classic ceiling of pure project consulting — bound by the time of one person. Raising fees alone hits buyer resistance well below the $1M+ target. Working more days erodes lifestyle and ultimately leads to burnout. Hiring junior consultants breaks the solo model and adds overhead Weiss explicitly warns against. The leverage shift is the only durable path: ADD revenue streams (retainers, products, IP licensing, cohorts) that compound without consuming more of your hours. Most stuck-at-$700K consultants are 95%+ project — that concentration IS the problem.",
